995
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:52,197
ROBERT:
I think for many Polish people,

996
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:54,825
especially in, you know, 1980s,

997
00:49:55,033 --> 00:49:56,576
when they hear songs
like "Powerslave"

998
00:49:56,743 --> 00:49:59,371
they could really refer this

999
00:49:59,413 --> 00:50:02,040
to their own situation
and the country's situation.

1000
00:50:02,124 --> 00:50:04,543
NEWSREADER: In Gdansk, some
muted shouts of Solidarity,

1001
00:50:04,710 --> 00:50:06,962
but enough police to ensure
there was no trouble.

1002
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:09,589
I think anybody
who's in a situation

1003
00:50:09,756 --> 00:50:11,925
where they're oppressed,

1004
00:50:12,968 --> 00:50:16,013
music is an outlet for people
to get them through hard times.

1005
00:50:17,305 --> 00:50:19,141
It's fantastic if you feel that

1006
00:50:19,349 --> 00:50:21,018
you've helped people
in that way.

1007
00:50:22,227 --> 00:50:23,311
We're not political.

1008
00:50:23,478 --> 00:50:25,897
We do it through the lyrics
of the music.

1009
00:50:25,981 --> 00:50:27,399
And that breaks down

1010
00:50:27,441 --> 00:50:29,860
the totalitarian barriers
around the world.

1011
00:50:45,542 --> 00:50:49,880
BRUCE: ♪ Tell me why
I had to be a Powerslave

1012
00:50:52,215 --> 00:50:56,845
♪ I don't wanna die
I'm a god, why can't I live on?

1013
00:50:58,221 --> 00:51:00,348
DR LINA KHATIB:
I first encountered Iron Maiden

1014
00:51:00,432 --> 00:51:02,976
when I was a teenager
in Lebanon.

1015
00:51:03,143 --> 00:51:06,229
In the early '90s, Lebanon had
just come out of civil war

1016
00:51:06,438 --> 00:51:09,066
and I had just discovered
heavy metal.

1017
00:51:09,274 --> 00:51:12,277
So I went to my local
bootleg record store

1018
00:51:12,319 --> 00:51:15,072
'cause that's all you had
in Lebanon at the time.

1019
00:51:15,155 --> 00:51:19,618
And I said, "I want the most
metal thing you have."

1020
00:51:19,701 --> 00:51:23,413
And he gave me... It was 1992,
he gave me Fear of the Dark.

1021
00:51:25,499 --> 00:51:28,710
And it was as if the album
was talking to me.

1022
00:51:28,835 --> 00:51:29,836
I mean, I was a teenager,

1023
00:51:30,003 --> 00:51:31,630
I'd just lived through war

1024
00:51:31,755 --> 00:51:34,466
in a country that was
still very turbulent,

1025
00:51:34,549 --> 00:51:36,551
and of course, like all art,

1026
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:38,762
the interpretation
is very subjective

1027
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:40,722
to the person
encountering that art.

1028
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:43,934
And so for me
listening to that album,

1029
00:51:44,017 --> 00:51:47,437
I just cast all kinds of
interpretations that had to do

1030
00:51:47,562 --> 00:51:49,648
with my own life
in war-time Lebanon.

1031
00:51:49,731 --> 00:51:51,358
And I felt this album

1032
00:51:51,483 --> 00:51:54,986
is basically commenting
on my life.

1033
00:51:55,112 --> 00:51:59,491
And that for me was very special
and it remains still today a...

1034
00:51:59,616 --> 00:52:02,828
a chilling experience
whenever I listen to it.

1035
00:52:02,953 --> 00:52:05,455
REPORTER: This is Mijalic
and these are the men

1036
00:52:05,580 --> 00:52:07,457
who come to burn it.

1037
00:52:07,499 --> 00:52:10,168
The Serbs call it
ethnic cleansing

1038
00:52:10,252 --> 00:52:13,505
and Mijalic's Muslims have fled.

1039
00:52:13,672 --> 00:52:16,007
SENAD SABOVIC: In the '90s,
the situation in Kosovo,

1040
00:52:16,174 --> 00:52:19,678
it was really bad.
You know, former Yugoslavia

1041
00:52:19,803 --> 00:52:23,723
and the ethno-nationalist wars
that... that ended it

1042
00:52:23,849 --> 00:52:26,977
was exactly the context of
me getting into Iron Maiden.

1043
00:52:28,478 --> 00:52:31,815
During the war there was
this community exchanging tapes.

1044
00:52:31,940 --> 00:52:34,526
These exchanges built
a community.

1045
00:52:34,609 --> 00:52:37,404
You know, you would just stay
friends with these people.

1046
00:52:37,571 --> 00:52:40,574
Through Iron Maiden I found
a community that is like-minded

1047
00:52:40,740 --> 00:52:43,743
and that bonded us further
together and kind of helped us

1048
00:52:43,827 --> 00:52:45,495
throughout the times
of hardship.

1049
00:52:47,914 --> 00:52:50,584
ROB FESTA: On September 11th,
we ended up responding

1050
00:52:50,667 --> 00:52:53,545
down to the site
at ground zero.

1051
00:52:53,712 --> 00:52:55,505
Saw the second one come down.
And that...

1052
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,593
You know, again,
seeing that come down,

1053
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:03,013
and even prior to that,
people jumping,

1054
00:53:04,472 --> 00:53:08,393
I needed an escape.
So, you can drink,

1055
00:53:08,560 --> 00:53:10,353
you could do things
that aren't good for you,

1056
00:53:10,520 --> 00:53:13,023
or you could find something that
you enjoy

1057
00:53:13,106 --> 00:53:15,901
that takes you to a different
place, to a better place.

1058
00:53:15,984 --> 00:53:17,110
For me, that was music.

1059
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:18,862
For me, that was
Iron Maiden's music.

1060
00:53:20,947 --> 00:53:23,700
DR KHATIB: People want to
feel that they belong somewhere

1061
00:53:23,783 --> 00:53:27,037
and so metal becomes
this feeling of belonging

1062
00:53:27,162 --> 00:53:29,873
to something where everyone
is equal,

1063
00:53:29,998 --> 00:53:33,501
where you are free to express
yourself, and crucially,

1064
00:53:33,585 --> 00:53:35,879
where you are defying
the system.

1065
00:53:36,004 --> 00:53:40,550
♪ Tell me why I had to be
a Powerslave

1066
00:53:42,969 --> 00:53:47,057
♪ I don't wanna die
I'm a god, why can't I live on?

1067
00:53:49,434 --> 00:53:55,982
♪ When the life giver dies
all around is laid waste

1068
00:53:56,149 --> 00:53:58,068
♪ And in my last hour

1069
00:53:58,109 --> 00:54:01,613
♪ I'm a slave
to the power of death

1070
00:54:01,738 --> 00:54:05,158
♪ Slave to the power of death

1071
00:54:05,242 --> 00:54:12,582
♪ Slave to the power of death

